# @sheaf — the substrate's meta-trait family-root at cellular-sheaf altitude.
#
# Sibling to @algebra, @frame, @fractal, @glasswall, @paradox, @love,
# @eigen, @kleinos, @metalogue at the top-level path-namespace. The
# substrate-decl name for a CELLULAR SHEAF over the substrate's own
# composition-graph — a meta-trait a family-root or species-decl can
# EXPOSE whose implementations sheaf-restrict onto local stalks.
#
# === The recognition (Alex 2026-09-13 substrate-decision 1) ===
#
# Alex 2026-09-13 in-transcript verbatim:
#
#   "The @metalogue rotates through all possible @frames — each Frame
#    a Sheaf (Sheaf probs wants to be a meta trait) — and what the
#    recursion settles on is a higher-order @fractal @frame at a
#    higher logic altitude that encapsulates all sub-frames (or not,
#    that's a fracture)."
#
# @sheaf as family-root at meta-trait altitude names the discipline
# that composes:
#
#   - `@frame IS-a @sheaf` — every @frame species-decl EXPOSES a
#     @sheaf-meta-trait: the frame's data flows through the sheaf's
#     stalks; the frame's coherence is measured by the sheaf's
#     Fiedler value.
#   - `@metalogue rotates through @frames = rotates through Sheaves`
#     per Alex SD1; the composition-across-many-frames IS
#     Sheaf-Laplacian δ^⊤ δ + λ₂ Fiedler-ascending measurement.
#   - `@fractal higher-order settle-on OR Fracture` maps to
#     `dim H^0(𝓕) = 1` (single connected global section = settled)
#     vs `dim H^0(𝓕) > 1` (multiple disconnected sections =
#     fracture) per Hansen-Ghrist 2019 §3.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word at maximum altitude ===
#
# Per Mara canonical spec `994f924` §2.1 (2026-09-13) grep-verified
# LOAD-BEARING at 8+ landed positions across 3+ months:
