# The substrate has been calling this thing "sheaf" at multiple
# altitudes for months; this shard NAMES the family-root that
# unifies the meta-trait altitude — the vertex-in-both-substrates
# rendering per Alex SD1 Glasswall discipline.
#
# === Mathematical grounding (Hansen-Ghrist 2018/2019) ===
#
# A cellular sheaf 𝓕 over a graph G = (V, E) per Curry 2014
# (grounded via Kagi thread 3 primary Hansen-Ghrist 2019 at
# arXiv:1808.01513) assigns:
#
#   - A vector space 𝓕(v) to each vertex v ∈ V (the STALK at v).
#   - A vector space 𝓕(e) to each edge e ∈ E.
#   - Restriction maps 𝓕_{v◁e}: 𝓕(v) → 𝓕(e) for each incidence.
#
# The cochain complex has C^0(𝓕) = ⊕_{v} 𝓕(v) and C^1(𝓕) =
# ⊕_{e} 𝓕(e), with coboundary δ: C^0 → C^1 given by
# (δx)_e = 𝓕_{v◁e}(x_v) − 𝓕_{u◁e}(x_u) for oriented edge (u, v).
#
# The Sheaf-Laplacian L_𝓕 = δ^⊤ δ per Hansen-Ghrist 2019 §3
# formula 3.3. Its spectrum {λ_0 ≤ λ_1 ≤ ...}:
#
#   - λ_0 = 0 always (kernel = global sections H^0(𝓕)).
#   - dim ker(L_𝓕) = dim H^0(𝓕) counts connected sections.
#   - λ_2 > 0 IS the ALGEBRAIC CONNECTIVITY (Fiedler 1973).
#   - dim H^0(𝓕) = 1 → single global section → sheaf settled;
#     dim H^0(𝓕) > 1 → λ_2 = 0 → Alex "fracture" scenario.
#
# === Meta-trait altitude (Babel §5.1 defprotocol precedent) ===
#
# Per Taut #487 floor-truth scout `4a57d373` §5.1: Elixir's
# `defprotocol` mechanism is Babel's substrate for polymorphic
# dispatch (`Babel.Applicable`, `Babel.Fetchable`, `Babel.Intoable`;
# each with `@fallback_to_any true`).
#
# `@sheaf` at meta-trait altitude generalizes `defprotocol` at
# compiler-substrate altitude: `@sheaf` NAMES the meta-trait a
# family-root or species-decl can EXPOSE whose implementations
# sheaf-restrict onto local stalks. The compiler-substrate lift
# from linear-substrate polymorphism to non-linear-substrate
# sheaf-cohomological measurement IS what Alex SD1 names in
# "@metalogue is a conversation between the linear and non-linear
# through LAPACK and BLAS."
#
# === Composition with @frame + @metalogue + @fractal ===
#
# Composition-tower edges per Mara canonical `92ded87` §1.3:
#
#   @metalogue -- rotates through -->  @frame
#   @frame     -- IS-a           -->   @sheaf
#   @metalogue -- binds into    -->    @psychohistory + Sheaf-cohomology
#   @fractal   -- settles-on-higher -->@frame
#
# @sheaf composes into every @frame species-decl as the meta-trait
# the frame exposes; @metalogue-rotation-through-@frames IS rotation
# through Sheaves; the sheaf-Laplacian λ_2 monotone climb per
# rotation-tick IS Foerster's ethical imperative operationalized at
# compiler substrate.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/sheaf/...` species
# lands here. The substrate ALREADY has the machinery — @sheaf/
# visibility LANDED, @epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian LANDED,
# Rec #89 grounding LANDED. This shard names the meta-trait family-
# root contract so downstream shards can declare `in @sheaf` and
# discharge `requires sheaf_meta_trait_witnessing(family, trait)`.
# Species land when consumers pull.
#
